            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Spanish for to pay in, then the Spanish for the pension."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: rico",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "rico — \"rich; tasty\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Es un país rico. It is a rich country."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With ser it means rich; with estar it means tasty: la sopa está muy rica."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "rico was borrowed from Gothic reiks 'mighty, powerful', from Germanic rīkijaz (EtymDB); being powerful came to mean having money."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
